  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tretamine may interact with Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 6A2, mitochondrial through multiple pathways. The drug targets several enzymes, including Methionine aminopeptidase 2 and Molybdopterin synthase catalytic subunit, which in turn target the same mitochondrial enzyme. This indicates that Tretamine could exert its effects by modulating the activity of this critical mitochondrial protein, potentially through different molecular mechanisms. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent relationship, with varying levels of confidence in the evidence. The overlapping targets imply that Tretamine might influence mitochondrial function by affecting the activity of this subunit, which is involved in the electron transport chain and energy production. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism by which Tretamine could interact with the mitochondrial enzyme, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
